WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.440
Yume kara samete mo
Even if I wake from my dreams

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.810
Kono te wo nobasu yo
I'll reach my hand out to you

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:28.800
Onaji tsuyosa de yobi au
If our hearts can reach each other

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:34.160
Kokoro ni nareru no naraba
with the same strength

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:40.670
Nanninbun no kizu demo
Then I would be able to bare

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:46.340
Boku wa uketome rareru yo
The pain of many hearts

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:50.280
Mousukoshi datte kiga surun da
I can feel that it will arrive soon

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:55.290
Kono kabe ga kuzureru
When these walls will be torn down

00:00:56.090 --> 00:01:00.430
Reimei
The dawn

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:08.130
Yume kara samete mo
mada minai yume no houmade
Even if we wake from our dreams
We'll have to keep running

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:14.110
Bokura wa hitori de
hashiri tsuzukeru shika nain da
Towards our unrevealed dreams

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:20.740
Korogari mayotte tsukuri dasu
boku no inryoku ga
The gravity by my painful journey
will draw me

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:27.020
Itsuka kimi e
To you one day

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.370
Shino...

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:19.240
Do you have a minute?

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:22.780
Didn't you quit the game?

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:25.680
After hearing about Shino...

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.580
...I started wondering if I should quit.

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:35.350
That's why I'm dragging my feet.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.360
Hey, what did happen?

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:43.290
I don't know anything beyond the rumors.

00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:46.940
I'm here because I'm concerned
about those rumors.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.370
Um...

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:51.570
Where's Haseo?

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:56.680
Did Haseo say anything?

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:00.150
Why don't you ask him yourself?

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.050
Haseo won't talk about it.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.920
With me, anyway.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:14.830
I hope I wasn't a bother.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:15.870
Sorry.

00:03:16.370 --> 00:03:20.200
You're the only one that can be
by his side now.

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.070
Ask him yourself.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:23.870
That's best.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:44.420
Go on and tie up all these veins

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:50.440
These red threads sewn through my flesh

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:56.340
Their dizzying length

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:59.310
Measures the distance to you

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.070
Thick, thin, hot and hard

00:04:02.150 --> 00:04:14.150
If you refer to this with
an elegant word like love

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:26.070
What is bared and revealed is unclean

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:36.710
This cracking and shattering death

00:04:40.350 --> 00:04:41.320
Shino...

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:45.220
Why won't you log in?

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.820
Why won't you answer your cell phone?

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:58.560
Ovan!

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:02.840
What are you doing at a time like this?

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:05.210
Where did you go?

00:05:05.210 --> 00:05:05.610
If you refer to this with
an elegant word like love
Where did you go?

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:17.080
If you refer to this with
an elegant word like love

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:28.090
Carrying the burden of this suffering

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:38.270
So, it's this sector.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:41.940
I've tried it three times.
It's the same sector I can't analyze.

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:45.340
Master Yata?

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:47.920
Which data is it that you can't analyze?

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:52.050
If it's all random data,
it can't be analyzed.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:54.110
You're forgetting the presupposition.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:56.990
If this is random junk data...

00:05:57.800 --> 00:06:00.660
...then Ovan's escape cannot be explained.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:02.190
I understand that.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:03.530
So?

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.900
The other possibility is that...

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:09.910
...this is something built by
a logic architecture unknown to us.

00:06:09.970 --> 00:06:11.670
Sounds like science fiction.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:15.240
But that kind of data actually exists here.

00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:16.570
And also...

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:18.650
What?

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:21.080
If you're going to use
the term "science fiction"...

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:26.190
...remember that online gaming itself
used to be science fiction.

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.360
We've just discovered...

00:06:31.230 --> 00:06:34.630
...the existence of an entity...

00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:38.230
...that we've never come across
here in The World.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.860
And we've confirmed that this entity
has attached itself...

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:43.700
...to Ovan's PC body.

00:06:44.780 --> 00:06:47.470
Then we need to find out what it is...

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:50.340
...and also confirm
its relationship to "the Factor".

00:06:50.580 --> 00:06:51.240
Don't we?

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:53.820
Pi?

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:54.580
Yes.

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:56.620
The rest depends on your actions.

00:06:57.690 --> 00:06:58.350
Yes.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:07.510
When did you last see Shino?

00:08:09.060 --> 00:08:10.530
That's worrisome.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.320
I finally found you!

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:24.490
I looked for you everywhere.

00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:36.410
Hey, that Sign...

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:42.950
I heard it appeared when Shino got killed.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:45.480
And if it did?

00:09:45.660 --> 00:09:48.960
You were there, right?

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:52.220
Yeah, I was.

00:09:55.330 --> 00:09:56.990
I couldn't do anything.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:59.400
Absolutely nothing.

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:02.800
Maybe if I'd contacted you sooner...

00:10:03.510 --> 00:10:04.840
...it would've been different.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.340
It had nothing to do with it.

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:07.240
But...

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.070
Sorry, my phone...

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:10.410
My cell's ringing.

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:15.050
Shino.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:18.390
Haseo...

00:10:18.790 --> 00:10:20.160
...what'd you say?

00:10:21.460 --> 00:10:22.950
What about Shino?!

00:10:27.170 --> 00:10:28.130
Haseo?

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:39.680
What's wrong?

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:43.040
There's something strange
about you, Phyllo.

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:47.580
Did you see Haseo?

00:10:48.890 --> 00:10:51.120
That's why I came here.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:53.490
Phyllo, are you okay?

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:55.390
Actually...

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:59.500
I'm not that okay.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:03.200
Can I stay here?

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.230
Did something happen?

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:12.100
If that really was Tri-Edge...

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:14.670
...we're in trouble.

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:18.420
You met him?

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:21.520
Yes.

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:37.760
She's late.

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:39.170
Oh, you're here.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.270
It's you, right?

00:11:45.580 --> 00:11:47.200
Why'd you come from over there?

00:11:47.280 --> 00:11:50.480
I got here early, so I wandered
over to the Beast Temple.

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:52.610
If you were to visit Minato-Mirai...

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:55.620
...it's not much of a stretch
to check out Chinatown as well.

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:58.880
Anyway, this meeting place is way too far.

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:00.580
You haven't changed.

00:12:00.660 --> 00:12:03.220
Well, the PC body may be different...

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:04.730
...but the inside's still the same.

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:06.090
That doesn't change.

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:09.530
Since you came here using
that character...

00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:12.430
...can I assume you're accepting my offer?

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:14.290
I like this one!

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:18.010
I mean, I wouldn't be comfortable
with my previous character.

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:19.470
But...

00:12:19.540 --> 00:12:20.480
But?

00:12:20.550 --> 00:12:22.910
I don't want to go back into
the secret service.

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:25.380
There is no TaN, you know.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:28.440
Therefore, there is no secret service either.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:30.340
There's no going back.

00:12:30.890 --> 00:12:32.010
Then, why?

00:12:32.660 --> 00:12:36.920
What are you trying to get me to do
by giving me a new PC body?

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:41.320
I won't make you break the terms of use,
so don't worry.

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:43.030
Sounds dangerous.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:46.960
This character has already
broken the rules, right?

00:12:47.270 --> 00:12:48.570
So, the question is...

00:12:48.640 --> 00:12:51.630
...whether or not you
can deal with that. That's all.

00:12:53.110 --> 00:12:54.300
I'll be in touch.

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:58.680
Your name...

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:00.640
Are you going to stick with Saburou?

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.610
That I won't give up.

00:13:02.690 --> 00:13:06.020
Even if the revisions have changed
and the game is different...

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:08.750
..."The World" hasn't changed.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:09.920
It's the same as that.

00:13:09.990 --> 00:13:11.550
I don't really get it.

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:14.230
But if you don't mind, then that's fine.

00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:57.300
What do you think you're doing?

00:13:57.810 --> 00:14:02.140
Why'd we meet in the dungeon,
only to be seen together here?

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:03.470
Oh, right.

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:08.040
But we don't need to sneak around
if we're not the secret service.

00:14:08.150 --> 00:14:09.980
You know what...

00:14:11.160 --> 00:14:12.320
So, what do you want?

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:13.580
Tri-Edge.

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:17.930
So you have something to do with him?

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:20.900
Maybe I do, and maybe I don't.

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:24.730
The rumors livening up the forum
have got me worried lately.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:28.140
But to be honest, I don't know right now.

00:14:28.510 --> 00:14:29.500
One more thing.

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:32.910
Isn't there going to be an event soon?

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.110
The one offered for a limited time?

00:14:35.180 --> 00:14:37.110
"Forest of Pain" right?

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:38.380
Yeah, that one.

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:41.580
Are you guys involved in it?

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:44.480
Who do you think we are?

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:48.420
We don't have the power to
interfere in an event...

00:14:48.490 --> 00:14:50.120
...controlled by the CC Corp.

00:14:50.190 --> 00:14:51.250
I wonder.

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:56.260
A girl who dreams of becoming
a singer might actually...

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:59.460
...live next door to an old man
who's actually a famous composer.

00:14:59.540 --> 00:15:02.010
I told you, I don't get your metaphors.

00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:06.370
Well, it seems pretty interesting,
so I'll use this body.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:07.100
Thanks!

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:08.640
Stay in touch.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:23.860
Where were you?

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:26.060
I'm not an NPC.

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:28.190
I have a real life, too.

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:31.030
It's not unusual for me to leave sometimes.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:33.290
What happened to you?

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:36.070
It's not even bedtime yet.

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:38.140
Um...

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:41.300
Never mind. Next time.

00:15:43.510 --> 00:15:44.480
Hey?

00:15:44.550 --> 00:15:45.520
What?

00:15:46.220 --> 00:15:49.120
What do you think of the rumors in the forum?

00:15:49.390 --> 00:15:50.980
There are a million rumors.

00:15:51.060 --> 00:15:52.520
Which one are you talking about?

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:53.980
Haven't you seen it?

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:56.080
Well, which one?

00:15:56.360 --> 00:16:01.060
The one saying that PC's killed
by Tri-Edge are lost.

00:16:02.630 --> 00:16:05.160
The real players lose consciousness.

00:16:09.240 --> 00:16:11.330
They become a Lost One.

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:15.810
What about Shino?

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.780
I wasn't talking about Shino!

00:16:18.050 --> 00:16:18.980
So?

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:22.280
Let's go somewhere else.
Come with me.

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:48.600
What is this place?

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:51.570
This is where I met Tri-Edge.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:52.410
Huh?

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:55.320
You defeated Tri-Edge?

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:58.480
No.

00:16:58.720 --> 00:17:03.590
But I thought you're done for
if you meet him.

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:06.060
Yes, that's right.

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:07.560
I don't understand!

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:09.100
Then, why?

00:17:12.540 --> 00:17:13.330
Haseo?

00:17:13.400 --> 00:17:14.030
What?

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:15.300
Tri-Edge...

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.570
...didn't see me as a worthy opponent.

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:15.930
I don't know why, but he spared me.

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:18.100
Does that kind of thing happen?

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:20.360
I just told you that it did.

00:18:21.340 --> 00:18:23.330
Then why did he kill Shino?

00:18:29.550 --> 00:18:30.950
Where is Shino?

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:32.940
Shino's...

00:18:33.780 --> 00:18:34.980
The real Shino's...

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:37.180
...unconscious.

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:40.520
She's in a hospital bed.

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:43.480
She...

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:48.630
The way she died wasn't normal.

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:56.000
I called her right away.

00:18:56.710 --> 00:18:57.500
Come on!

00:18:57.680 --> 00:18:58.840
Answer your phone!

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:04.840
Then I got a phone call from her mother.

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:08.210
So she found your number
on the call history?

00:19:09.790 --> 00:19:12.810
Shino lives by herself,
and when her friends...

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:16.860
...started to think something was wrong,
they called her parents.

00:19:16.930 --> 00:19:18.550
It was a huge commotion.

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:20.460
She...

00:19:20.760 --> 00:19:21.730
Huh?

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:27.170
Until the landlord opened the door...

00:19:27.240 --> 00:19:30.760
...and called the ambulance,
she was alone in her room.

00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:33.640
All by herself.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:37.770
If her friends hadn't called...

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:41.050
What did her mother say?

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:46.220
She said I must know something
about why this happened.

00:19:49.490 --> 00:19:51.430
Like it was my fault.

00:19:53.430 --> 00:19:55.190
It must have been tough on you.

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:57.400
But it is.

00:19:58.770 --> 00:19:59.790
Haseo?

00:20:00.240 --> 00:20:01.700
It is my fault!

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:04.410
Because...

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:09.840
...if I'd gotten to the cathedral sooner...

00:20:10.150 --> 00:20:11.550
It would have been the same.

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:15.020
At worst, you may have become
another Lost One.

00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:16.020
But!

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:20.520
If that was Tri-Edge
you are no match for him.

00:20:26.360 --> 00:20:30.230
So is this a special field or something?

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:33.890
It's a normal field
as you can see, but...

00:20:34.300 --> 00:20:37.140
I can kind of understand
the Lost Grounds.

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:38.610
But why would he...

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:42.170
...Tri-Edge...

00:20:43.350 --> 00:20:45.140
...come to a place like this?

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:51.580
Why were you here?

00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:53.720
What?

00:20:53.790 --> 00:20:55.190
By chance.

00:20:55.760 --> 00:20:59.700
You're always in the Mac Anu canal area...

00:20:59.760 --> 00:21:02.160
...and you just came here "by chance"?

00:21:03.600 --> 00:21:05.800
Am I supposed to believe that?

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:08.570
Spit it out!

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:12.440
Ovan and Shino...

00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:18.680
...they met here.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:48.240
Become stronger.

00:22:29.590 --> 00:22:33.180
Ikiru wa dokuhai kiyu no kurushimi wo
Life is a poisoned cup of needless suffering

00:22:33.260 --> 00:22:36.690
Nomihosu sube wo dare ga sazukeyo
That no one can show me how to drain

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:40.360
Taiyo ni sumu toiu kenja no washi
A wise eagle is said to live in the sun

00:22:40.430 --> 00:22:44.800
Habataki dake ga kodama suru
The flapping of its wings
is all that echoes

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:51.770
Kono futatsu no me ni yadotta
In each of these eyes

00:22:51.840 --> 00:22:55.540
Yami to Hikari sono docchi de
Dwell darkness and light

00:22:55.610 --> 00:23:02.850
Boku wa ashita wo mitsumeru beki nano darou
Through which shall I look to tomorrow?

00:23:02.920 --> 00:23:06.580
Kawaki kitta gareki no machi
A dried out and ruined city

00:23:06.660 --> 00:23:10.350
Ten to sen wo tsunagi awase
Draws the lines between the dots

00:23:10.430 --> 00:23:17.360
Imi nado nai koto bakari afurete iku
Causing meaningless events to overflow

00:23:17.530 --> 00:23:21.270
Honou no gotoki kodoku
Soothing the loneliness

00:23:21.340 --> 00:23:24.360
Idaku karada shizumete wa
That flames up within the body

00:23:24.440 --> 00:23:31.970
Ankyo eto shitatatte iku shizuku
Droplets of water fall towards the culvert

00:23:32.220 --> 00:23:35.710
Kakageru dokuhai kono sei wa michitemo
Even if the poisoned cup is upheld
and filled with this life

00:23:35.820 --> 00:23:39.520
Kogareru shino yume wa nagare tsuku
My dream that yearns for death
drifts into it

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:43.220
Toride ni kuikomu tsume kokou no washi
The eagle remains aloof;
its talons dig into the fort

00:23:43.290 --> 00:23:46.790
Habataki dake ga maiagaru
Only the flapping of its wings resounds

00:23:46.860 --> 00:23:50.590
Ano soukyu ni takkei ni shite kure tamae
Let me be crucified in the blue sky

00:23:50.670 --> 00:23:54.360
Ten to chi ga musubu basho ni
bokuwa tatsu
I'll stand where heaven and earth meet

00:23:55.470 --> 00:23:56.940
Next Episode
